1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,591
Just make sure there's no evidence.

2
00:00:49,674 --> 00:00:52,927
A brokenhearted man and a grieving son
who just couldn't take it anymore.

3
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:55,096
They'll all think the same thing.

4
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,931
You can't make a mistake.

5
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,141
No one will ever know.

6
00:00:58,224 --> 00:00:59,517
End it well.

7
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:05,774
We already know who killed him.

8
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:06,775
So what's the problem?

9
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:08,985
Dad is gone. He can't tell us
what he wants anymore.

10
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:12,363
So don't use his name to justify

11
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:16,326
something that you want to do.

12
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:18,995
<i>You want me to kill Brother Mikoy?</i>

13
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,789
If Sianong fails,

14
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:35,011
Carlota.

15
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:37,222
Don't talk to me.

16
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:38,515
We're done.

17
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:39,390
Sianong!

18
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:43,311
Let Carlota go.

19
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:44,729
No one's going to chase you.

20
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:45,855
Let her go.

21
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,325
- Carlota.
- Run after him!

22
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:03,623
I'm still wondering how
Agent Sianong did that.

23
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:04,874
Me too, I still can't understand.

24
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:08,002
I don't know why we have to guard him.

25
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:11,881
And why he had to betray us.

26
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:14,801
Remember, he likes to read that book--
What is it again?

27
00:02:53,548 --> 00:02:54,716
Yes.

28
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:57,510
I still can't believe he did that.

29
00:02:58,177 --> 00:02:59,429
What did you think?

30
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:00,388
I don't know.

31
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:03,933
Have you seen Sianong?

32
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:07,186
Ma'am, we've been here for a while,
and we haven't seen him.

33
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,563
Alex.

34
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:10,481
He might have gone through here.

35
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:11,482
Let's go.

36
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:13,443
Stay here and let us know if you see him.

37
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:14,736
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay, ma'am.

38
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:18,615
Cocoy.

39
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:20,658
- Wake up.
- Ouch!

40
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:23,077
Easy.

41
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,454
What happened?

42
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:27,665
Where's Sianong?

43
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:28,833
It was him.

44
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:30,752
He's the mole.

45
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:36,674
Where is he?

46
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:38,092
He escaped.

47
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:42,222
How about Mikoy?

48
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:43,765
He's with Alex.

49
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:45,016
They're after him.

50
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:06,371
Yes?

51
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:11,876
What happened?

52
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:15,129
Mikoy is still alive.

53
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:18,549
How?

54
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,552
I just got a little too complacent,

55
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:24,639
and there was also
a lack of judgment on my end.

56
00:04:25,348 --> 00:04:28,977
Maybe that's why
they kind of outsmarted me.

57
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,561
A little?

58
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:41,864
Alex, go ahead.

59
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:43,658
I'll stay here for now. I'll follow you.

60
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:44,784
Okay.

61
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:53,459
They're after me.

62
00:05:03,886 --> 00:05:04,846
Vicky!

63
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:06,639
What do you mean?

64
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:09,350
You know what I mean.

65
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,229
I don't understand what you're saying.

66
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:20,403
After everything I've done for you,
for this mission,

67
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,280
for your grand mission, Vicky.

68
00:05:27,201 --> 00:05:28,328
Do you know what I did?

69
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:30,288
I fucked everything up for this mission.

70
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:31,581
I fucked over the agency.

71
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:35,126
I fucked over everyone who cared about me.

72
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:37,253
And you knew all the risks!

73
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:43,551
So what now?

74
00:05:44,343 --> 00:05:45,303
That's it?

75
00:05:46,387 --> 00:05:47,889
Was that all for nothing?

76
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:51,642
No one forced you.

77
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:53,061
You chose this.

78
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:56,606
Because you made me feel
like I mattered, Vicky.

79
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:58,775
That I could take revenge for Alice.

80
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:02,070
That everything we were doing
would lead to something.

81
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:03,696
That it would go somewhere,

82
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:06,908
and that I was part of all this.

83
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:08,201
You mattered

84
00:06:08,284 --> 00:06:10,244
when you were still useful to me.

85
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:13,122
Vicky!

86
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:14,916
This is where it ends, Sianong.

87
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,126
No, Vicky.

88
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,294
Vicky.

89
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:53,496
Surrender now.

90
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:01,087
Come with us and face what you've done.

91
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:05,007
You have nowhere else to go.

92
00:07:31,367 --> 00:07:32,326
Sianong, that's enough!

93
00:07:33,995 --> 00:07:34,912
Alex!

94
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:41,919
Bok, that's enough!

95
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,432
Mom?

96
00:07:54,515 --> 00:07:56,601
- We need to leave.
- Why?

97
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:57,894
We're compromised.

98
00:07:57,977 --> 00:07:58,978
How about Sianong?

99
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:00,688
We'll deal with him later.

100
00:08:00,771 --> 00:08:01,939
What if he talks?

101
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:05,193
He already knows
what will happen to him if he does.

102
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:07,195
Let's go. Get your things.

103
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:14,368
What now, Mikoy?

104
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:20,041
Sianong.

105
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,002
It doesn't have to end this way.

106
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,259
You're angry?

107
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:38,476
Think about Chiara.

108
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,062
Think about your father!

109
00:08:53,324 --> 00:08:54,242
What?

110
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,997
you still can't hurt me?

111
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:04,919
That's enough, Bok!

112
00:09:06,462 --> 00:09:07,588
I don't want to hurt you.

113
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:17,181
Oh, really? Huh?

114
00:09:26,899 --> 00:09:27,900
Sianong!

115
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:30,945
Sianong! Hold on!

116
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:32,446
Why?

117
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:37,076
Why are you saving me?

118
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:39,078
What kind of question is that?!

119
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:40,288
Help me!

120
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:42,957
Hold on!

121
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:45,918
Sianong!

122
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:48,254
Hold on!

123
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:49,380
Bok.

124
00:09:56,095 --> 00:09:57,972
There's no going back for me, Bok.

125
00:09:58,055 --> 00:10:00,349
No! There is! Just hold on!

126
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:05,271
I know you two are my friends.

127
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,606
Right?

128
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:08,649
But I screwed you both.

129
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:09,900
That's enough!

130
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,944
Give me one of your hands.
Reach it out to me, please!

131
00:10:12,028 --> 00:10:13,112
Reach it out, Sianong!

132
00:10:13,195 --> 00:10:14,113
Mikoy.

133
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:16,991
It's not too late for Chiara.

134
00:10:18,951 --> 00:10:22,079
Chiara isn't the one
who's responsible for all of this.

135
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:26,250
It's Vicky.

136
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:29,462
Vicky is behind all of this.

137
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:32,131
You two go to Italy!

138
00:10:32,965 --> 00:10:34,925
Can you do that later, Sianong?

139
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:36,135
Hold on!

140
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:39,013
Hold on!

141
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:40,848
Sianong.

142
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:44,977
- Sianong.
- Bok.

143
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:51,067
- Sianong, hold on.
- But…

144
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,610
I'm tired.

145
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:58,574
Sianong!

146
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,159
Sianong, don't!

147
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:01,077
Don't do that!

148
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:03,037
Sianong!

149
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:08,834
Sianong!

150
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:13,005
Sianong!

151
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:20,030
I never thought Sianong's story
would end like this.

152
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:23,075
I'm not used to it.

153
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,201
The silence.

154
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:26,954
No one's correcting us anymore.

155
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:32,209
No one's suddenly going to say,
"According to the 7 habits."

156
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:36,005
Then it will lead
to a 20-minute discussion.

157
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:39,633
And somehow end up talking about
<i>Lord of the Rings</i>.

158
00:12:43,762 --> 00:12:46,223
Everything somehow ends up
with him talking about <i>Lord of the Rings</i>.

159
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:54,732
He always used to tell me

160
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:57,359
to think first.

161
00:12:59,361 --> 00:13:00,905
Don't act rashly.

162
00:13:03,073 --> 00:13:04,366
Follow the plan.

163
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:07,203
Follow the rules.

164
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:12,833
It's annoying.

165
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:17,463
He was always right.

166
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:21,634
That's why I don't understand

167
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:24,512
why he let things get that far.

168
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:29,141
We couldn't sleep last night either.

169
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:32,019
Agent Alex and I went through everything.

170
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:34,104
The records he was involved in.

171
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:38,150
Just to see where we went wrong,

172
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:39,818
what we missed.

173
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:57,962
Do you know about Sianong?

174
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,764
Imagine,

175
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:11,600
she already had someone inside GAGO,

176
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:31,412
And that's what worries us, dear.

177
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:36,750
We don't know who her contacts are,

178
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:39,128
or how she got in, right?

179
00:14:40,045 --> 00:14:43,674
And who are the people working under her?

180
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:44,758
We have no idea.

181
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:59,899
Apparently, Sianong loved someone
who became a victim of human trafficking.

182
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:03,569
And he wasn't able to save her.

183
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,572
He wasn't able to get justice
for her either.

184
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:10,367
He never told me.

185
00:15:11,785 --> 00:15:13,329
None of us knew.

186
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:17,958
But what Sianong did was wrong.

187
00:15:18,542 --> 00:15:20,085
He betrayed us.

188
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:23,005
He tried to kill Mikoy.

189
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:26,967
But I don't want that to be
what we remember him by.

190
00:15:29,386 --> 00:15:30,930
Sianong was a good person.

191
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:34,266
He just lost his way.

192
00:15:37,269 --> 00:15:38,604
I wish he had told us.

193
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:43,609
I wish he had given us
a chance to help him.

194
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:49,031
But that doesn't justify betraying us.

195
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:51,408
It doesn't.

196
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:56,205
But that's the reason
why Vicky was able to use him.

197
00:15:57,289 --> 00:15:58,832
He was used as a weapon.

198
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:03,879
He was also a victim of a system that
made him believe he had no other choice.

199
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,840
I'm not saying what he did was right.

200
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:10,177
But if we don't want what happened
to Sianong to happen again,

201
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:12,513
we need to bring down the system

202
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:14,473
that creates people like him.

203
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:18,227
And the Concordat.

204
00:16:28,862 --> 00:16:29,780
Dear.

205
00:16:31,782 --> 00:16:34,743
If she can plant someone

206
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:36,453
inside GAGO,

207
00:16:38,163 --> 00:16:40,082
then she can also plant someone

208
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,376
right beside you.

209
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:53,012
What?

210
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:32,926
Wherever he is now,

211
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:37,014
I hope he found the peace

212
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:38,932
he couldn't find here.

213
00:17:40,851 --> 00:17:42,978
Before he let go, he told us something.

214
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:47,733
Let's go to Italy.

215
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:55,199
What's in Italy?

216
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:58,160
That's what we need to find out.

217
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:16,428
Nothing.

218
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:23,018
Absolutely nothing.

219
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:24,812
No contacts for Sianong there,

220
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:25,979
no accounts,

221
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:28,816
not even any recent travel records.

222
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:31,485
But he said it himself, Italy.

223
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,532
Maybe we're missing something.

224
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,326
Where's Carlota, by the way?

225
00:18:42,579 --> 00:18:43,580
Thank you.

226
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:58,053
Looks like you ordered enough
for an entire family.

227
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,472
Do you see a family here?

228
00:19:08,021 --> 00:19:09,189
Do you want to talk about it?

229
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,566
No.

230
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:22,369
I'm such an idiot.

231
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:25,289
I knew you wanted to talk about it.

232
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:33,338
I don't understand.

233
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:38,010
We went on so many dates.

234
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:41,054
We talked about so many things.

235
00:19:42,931 --> 00:19:45,475
I still don't know who he was.

236
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:47,227
Who he really was.

237
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:50,981
Some part of it must've been real.

238
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:54,401
Surely not all of it was a lie.

239
00:19:57,696 --> 00:19:59,156
He liked to make plans.

240
00:19:59,781 --> 00:20:00,824
Sianong?

241
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:06,205
He even made a list

242
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:09,082
of all the places he wanted to visit.

243
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:11,960
I even told him,

244
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:14,004
for our VL,

245
00:20:14,087 --> 00:20:16,715
he might as well turn it into
a project management plan.

246
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:22,429
What?

247
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:30,646
Definitely Italy.

248
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:39,071
What do you mean by that?

249
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:45,827
I thought you'd say New Zealand.

250
00:20:49,998 --> 00:20:51,750
So what are you going to do in Italy?

251
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,377
So many things!

252
00:20:58,048 --> 00:20:59,424
You already have an itinerary!

253
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,134
It's not an itinerary.

254
00:21:01,218 --> 00:21:02,386
It's a preliminary plan!

255
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:04,846
That's even worse!

256
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:09,643
No. I have some friends there too.

257
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:17,484
Castellanis?

258
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:18,944
Fancy!

259
00:21:19,611 --> 00:21:20,779
Don't worry.

260
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:24,032
One day, I'll take you there.

261
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:27,411
Really?

262
00:21:29,621 --> 00:21:30,664
How about now!

263
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:39,006
Castellani.

264
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:41,049
What?

265
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:43,885
Castellani!

266
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:50,267
Hey, wait. Who's paying for this?

267
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:54,896
I've figured it out.

268
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:57,274
Carlota?

269
00:21:57,357 --> 00:21:59,276
Now I know why in Italy.

270
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:00,902
Why?

271
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:02,821
Sianong has friends there.

272
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:05,240
The Castellanis.

273
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:06,700
Castellani?

274
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:10,454
The last thing he told me

275
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:14,458
was that he wanted to go to Italy
because he wanted to visit them.

276
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:17,461
If that's Sianong's last clue to us,

277
00:22:18,628 --> 00:22:21,548
those are the people he wants us to find.

278
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:55,874
<i>I have news about the Castellani.</i>

279
00:23:28,031 --> 00:23:31,952
it's impossible that we can persuade her
to come back to our country.

280
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:35,455
Didn't we agree
to bring Chiara Valtrovi back?

281
00:23:39,209 --> 00:23:40,085
What's the problem?

282
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:43,964
What did they say?

283
00:23:44,047 --> 00:23:47,050
They wanted to meet me. ASAP.

284
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:49,302
You know those Castellanis.
They are cunning.

285
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:51,429
They're cunning? That's their reputation.

286
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:52,639
We won't back out.

287
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:07,821
I know they are in Italy.

288
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:10,157
But Italy is too big,
and I don't have enough time.

289
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:12,576
If I have to know something
as soon as possible,

290
00:24:12,659 --> 00:24:13,827
then tell me now.

291
00:24:22,878 --> 00:24:24,379
Do not go, please.

292
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:33,263
I'm sure all of them are waiting
to see how I will handle this.
